  "editorial": "The known one-edit limit removes the need for a full distance table. At the first mismatch, the relative lengths determine which pointer advances; any later mismatch proves that more than one edit is required. End-of-string leftovers account for an insertion/deletion at the end. The independent oracle computes the full Levenshtein dynamic-programming table on small strings and checks whether the distance equals one. The returned Boolean and linear-time goal distinguish this exercise from the existing general edit-distance problem.",
